Project Planning Phase

The Project Planning Phase is the stage where we decide what to do, how to do it, when to do it, and who will do it.

Main Points:

Set Project Goals – Define the main objectives of the project.
Identify Tasks – Divide the project into smaller tasks and activities.
Allocate Resources – Decide the required people, software, hardware, and budget.
Create Timeline – Set deadlines and milestones for completing each task.
Assign Responsibilities – Decide which team member will handle each task.
